{
  // Pinned devbox GLOBAL manifest for the default worker toolchain (PRD #83 M1, Q2).
  //
  // go + python3 + pip are the owner's "the default worker should have docker/python/go
  // available" set. They are delivered through the ONE nix/devbox provisioning path
  // (PRD #18 — no second apk package path, no version drift), realized into the baked
  // image /nix at BUILD time via `devbox global install` so first use is instant instead
  // of paying the cold-start closure fetch. Each template Dockerfile copies this file
  // (agent/devbox-global/devbox.json) into devbox's global config dir and installs it
  // (base + jvm, in lockstep — jvm is NOT `FROM base`). It lives OUTSIDE agent/templates/
  // because that dir is one-directory-per-worker-image; this is shared build config, not
  // a template.
  //
  // devbox.json is parsed as HuJSON, so these `//` comments are valid.
  //
  // NOTE (pinning): the sibling `devbox.lock` pins the nixpkgs revision to an exact
  // COMMIT (generated by the tester's live arm64 build), so go/python/pip do
  // NOT drift per rebuild. Each Dockerfile COPYs the lock in BEFORE `devbox global install`
  // — without that COPY the image never sees it and the pin would float. Bump both the
  // manifest and the lock together when upgrading the toolchain.
  //
  // CORRECTION (2026-07-25, PRD #123): the line above read "an exact resolved store path".
  // It does not. Every entry in devbox.lock resolves to a FLAKE REF —
  // `github:NixOS/nixpkgs/20535e48…#<attr>` — not a `/nix/store/…` path; there is no
  // store_path key in the file at all. The distinction is load-bearing, not pedantic: a
  // store path would need no evaluation and therefore no github, whereas a flake ref means
  // nix must still evaluate nixpkgs, which is why PRD #123 treats "just commit a lockfile"
  // as an unproven spike rather than the obvious fix. The pin against DRIFT is real; the
  // pin against NETWORK is not what this file provides.
  //
  // `pip` is nixpkgs `python3Packages.pip` (there is no top-level `pip` attr); the tester
  // confirms `pip`/`python3`/`go` all resolve on the agent PATH of the built image (Q-C).
  //
  // `gcc` completes the go/python3 toolchains rather than being a repo-specific extra:
  // `go test -race` and cgo need a C compiler/linker (this repo's own store integration
  // tests run `-race`), and python C-extension wheels need one too. Delivered through the
  // SAME nix/devbox path as go so cgo links against the matching toolchain (an apk/musl
  // gcc would mismatch nix-glibc go). Validate `cgo`/`-race` in the built image.
  //
  // PRD #87 — the browser for the `web-ux` role rides this SAME shared toolchain (the
  // owner's chosen delivery), so it lands in every worker image (base + jvm) with one
  // manifest edit and no dedicated image variant:
  //   * `chromium` — the headless browser agent-browser drives (mainProgram `chromium`,
  //     so it resolves at /opt/uzi-toolchain/bin/chromium; AGENT_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_PATH
  //     in both Dockerfiles points there). Prebuilt in cache.nixos.org on x86_64-linux at
  //     the pinned rev (chromium-150.0.7871.128, narinfo HTTP 200), so CI's amd64-only
  //     kaniko build substitutes it rather than compiling Chromium from source.
  //   * `fontconfig` + `dejavu_fonts` — a nix Chromium closure ships NO fonts, so without
  //     a font package + a fontconfig that can find it every screenshot (the role's whole
  //     evidence artifact) renders tofu. Both prebuilt at the pinned rev. The Dockerfiles
  //     wire FONTCONFIG_FILE at /opt/uzi-toolchain/share/fonts and pre-warm the cache.
  // agent-browser itself is NOT a nix package — it is the pinned npm CLI in
  // agent/package.json (baked by `npm ci`), never installed per-run.
  //
  // `openssl` is a broadly-useful base crypto/TLS CLI (cert generation, `openssl rand`,
  // hashing, PEM/DER) that many repos' test harnesses and scripts reach for — the same
  // "every worker should have it" class as go/python3, NOT a repo-specific extra like a
  // Homebrew formula's ruby. It was first surfaced by uzi's own e2e harness
  // (e2e/run-e2e.sh forge-fake self-signed cert; judge rec, run dd06c0ed) but lives here
  // in the baked toolchain rather than as tier-2 so its absence never surfaces a silent
  // exit 127 to an agent in ANY repo. Its closure is small and largely already present
  // via the other packages' deps, so it adds negligible image weight.
  //
  // NOTE: it MUST be `openssl.bin`, not bare `openssl`. nixpkgs splits openssl into
  // outputs and its outputsToInstall is [bin, man] with NO `out`, so `devbox global
  // install` of bare `openssl` lands only libs/man and `command -v openssl` 127s — the
  // build guard then fails (proven: MR !103 pipeline 19969, build:agent). The `.bin`
  // output carries the `openssl` CLI; verified `devbox install` at the pinned rev puts
  // /opt/uzi-toolchain/bin/openssl on PATH. (gcc/go/python3 don't hit this — their CLI
  // is in `out`, which IS installed.)
  "packages": [
    "go",
    "gcc",
    "python3",
    "python3Packages.pip",
    "chromium",
    "fontconfig",
    "dejavu_fonts",
    "openssl.bin"
  ]
}
